   "evidence": "`Local.lean:286` reads `def interiorCoord {n : \u2115} (w ...) := euclideanHalfSpaceBoundaryNormalEquiv n (..., Real.log (w 0))`. Grepping the file for `interiorCoord` finds only the def, `interiorCoord_coe_interiorEmbedding` (292) and `contDiffOn_interiorCoord` (300), and the proof at line 294 unfolds the def with `rw [interiorCoord, ...]`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/Boundary/Collar/Local.lean",
   "fix": "Add an evaluation lemma, either `interiorCoord_def` or `@[simp]` coordinate lemmas `interiorCoord_apply_zero : interiorCoord w 0 = Real.log (w 0)` and `interiorCoord_apply_succ : interiorCoord w i.succ = w i.succ`. Also add `coe_interiorEmbedding_interiorCoord (hw : 0 < w 0) : (interiorEmbedding n (interiorCoord w)).1 = w`, so the two maps form an inverse pair on `{w | 0 < w 0}`.",
   "issue": "`interiorCoord` is a public def with no `@[expose]`, and its only characterizing lemma is the one-sided `interiorCoord_coe_interiorEmbedding`. There is no lemma that evaluates it and no reverse inverse: for `0 < w 0`, `(interiorEmbedding n (interiorCoord w)).1 = w`. The proofs in this file unfold it with `rw [interiorCoord]`, which importing modules cannot do.",
   "line": 286
  }
 ],
